// Xgesvdp computes the singular value decomposition (SVD) of an m×n matrix A and corresponding the left and/or right singular vectors.
//
// The SVD is written A=U*Σ*Vᴴ, where Σ is an m×n matrix which is zero except for its min(m,n) diagonal elements, U is an m×m unitary matrix, and V is an n×n unitary matrix. The diagonal elements of Σ are the singular values of A; they are real and non-negative, and are returned in descending order. The first min(m,n) columns of U and V are the left and right singular vectors of A.
// [Handle.Xgesvdp] combines polar decomposition in [14] and [Handle.Xsyevd] to compute SVD. It is much faster than [Handle.Xgesvd] which is based on QR algorithm. However polar decomposition in [14] may not deliver a full unitary matrix when the matrix A has a singular value close to zero. To workaround the issue when the singular value is close to zero, we add a small perturbation so polar decomposition can deliver the correct result. The consequence is inaccurate singular values shifted by this perturbation. The output parameter hErrSigma is the magnitude of this perturbation. In other words, hErrSigma shows the accuracy of SVD.
// The user has to provide device and host working spaces which are pointed by input parameters bufferOnDevice and bufferOnHost. The input parameters workspaceInBytesOnDevice (and workspaceInBytesOnHost) is size in bytes of the device (and host) working space, and it is returned by [Handle.XgesvdpBufferSize].
// If output parameter info = -i (less than zero), the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle).
// Currently, [Handle.Xgesvdp] supports only the default algorithm.
// Algorithms supported by [Handle.Xgesvdp]
//   - [Alg0], the zero value: Default algorithm.
//
// Please visit cuSOLVER Library Samples - [Handle.Xgesvdp] for a code example.
// Remark 1: gesvdp supports n>=m as well.
// Remark 2: the routine returns V, not Vᴴ
// The generic API has three different types, dataTypeA is data type of the matrix A, dataTypeS is data type of the vector S and dataTypeU is data type of the matrix U, dataTypeV is data type of the matrix V, computeType is compute type of the operation. [Handle.Xgesvdp] only supports the following four combinations:
// Valid combination of data type and compute type
//
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - jobz: Specifies options to either compute singular values only or compute singular vectors as well: jobz = [EigModeNovector] : Compute singular values only. jobz = [EigModeVector] : Compute singular values and singular vectors
//   - econ: econ = 1 for economy size for U and V
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: Array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,m). On exit, the contents of A are destroyed
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - dataTypeS: Data type of array S
//   - s: Real array of dimension min(m,n). The singular values of A, sorted so that S(i) >= S(i+1)
//   - dataTypeU: Data type of array U
//   - u: Array of dimension ldu * m with ldu is not less than max(1,m). U contains the m×m unitary matrix U. If econ=1, only reports first min(m,n) columns of U
//   - ldu: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix U
//   - dataTypeV: Data type of array V
//   - v: Array of dimension ldv * n with ldv is not less than max(1,n). V contains the n×n unitary matrix V. if econ=1, only reports first min(m,n) columns of V
//   - ldv: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix V
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - bufferOnDevice: Device workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnDevice bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size in bytes of bufferOnDevice, returned by [Handle.XgesvdpBufferSize]
//   - bufferOnHost: Host workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnHost bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size in bytes of bufferOnHost, returned by [Handle.XgesvdpBufferSize]
//   - hErrSigma: Magnitude of the perturbation, showing the accuracy of SVD
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( m,n<0 or lda<max(1,m) or ldu<max(1,m) or ldv<max(1,n)).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgesvdp.
func (h Handle) Xgesvdp(params Params, jobz EigMode, econ int32, m int64, n int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, dataTypeS DataType, s driver.DevicePtr, dataTypeU DataType, u driver.DevicePtr, ldu int64, dataTypeV DataType, v driver.DevicePtr, ldv int64, computeType DataType, bufferOnDevice driver.DevicePtr, workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, bufferOnHost uintptr, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint, dInfo driver.DevicePtr, hErrSigma *float64) error {
	return xgesvdp(h, params, jobz, econ, m, n, dataTypeA, a, lda, dataTypeS, s, dataTypeU, u, ldu, dataTypeV, v, ldv, computeType, bufferOnDevice, workspaceInBytesOnDevice, bufferOnHost, workspaceInBytesOnHost, dInfo, hErrSigma)
}

// XgesvdpBufferSize returns the workspace sizes, in bytes, for [Handle.Xgesvdp].
//
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - jobz: Specifies options to either compute singular values only or compute singular vectors as well: jobz = [EigModeNovector] : Compute singular values only. jobz = [EigModeVector] : Compute singular values and singular vectors
//   - econ: econ = 1 for economy size for U and V
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: Array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,m). On exit, the contents of A are destroyed
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - dataTypeS: Data type of array S
//   - s: Real array of dimension min(m,n). The singular values of A, sorted so that S(i) >= S(i+1)
//   - dataTypeU: Data type of array U
//   - u: Array of dimension ldu * m with ldu is not less than max(1,m). U contains the m×m unitary matrix U. If econ=1, only reports first min(m,n) columns of U
//   - ldu: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix U
//   - dataTypeV: Data type of array V
//   - v: Array of dimension ldv * n with ldv is not less than max(1,n). V contains the n×n unitary matrix V. if econ=1, only reports first min(m,n) columns of V
//   - ldv: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix V
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size of bufferOnDevice, in bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size of bufferOnHost, in bytes
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( m,n<0 or lda<max(1,m) or ldu<max(1,m) or ldv<max(1,n)).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgesvdpBufferSize, bound as cusolverDnXgesvdp_bufferSize.
func (h Handle) XgesvdpBufferSize(params Params, jobz EigMode, econ int32, m int64, n int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, dataTypeS DataType, s driver.DevicePtr, dataTypeU DataType, u driver.DevicePtr, ldu int64, dataTypeV DataType, v driver.DevicePtr, ldv int64, computeType DataType) (workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint, err error) {
	return xgesvdpBufferSize(h, params, jobz, econ, m, n, dataTypeA, a, lda, dataTypeS, s, dataTypeU, u, ldu, dataTypeV, v, ldv, computeType)
}

// Xgesvdr computes the approximated rank-k singular value decomposition (k-SVD) of an m×n matrix A and the corresponding left and/or right singular vectors.
//
// The k-SVD is written as Aₖ≈U*Σ*Vᴴ, where Σ is a k×k matrix which is zero except for its diagonal elements, U is an m×k orthonormal matrix, and V is an k×n orthonormal matrix. The diagonal elements of Σ are the approximated singular values of A; they are real and non-negative, and are returned in descending order. The columns of U and V are the top- k left and right singular vectors of A.
// [Handle.Xgesvdr] implements randomized methods described in [15] to compute k-SVD that is accurate with high probability if the conditions described in [15] hold. [Handle.Xgesvdr] is intended to compute a very small portion of the spectrum (meaning that k is very small compared to min(m,n)). of A fast and with good quality, specially when the dimensions of the matrix are large.
// The accuracy of the method depends on the spectrum of A, the number of power iterations niters, the oversampling parameter p and the ratio between p and the dimensions of the matrix A. Larger values of oversampling p or larger number of iterations niters might produce more accurate approximations, but it will also increase the run time of [Handle.Xgesvdr].
// Our recommendation is to use two iterations and set the oversampling to at least 2k. Once the solver provides enough accuracy, adjust the values of k and niters for better performance.
// The user has to provide device and host working spaces which are pointed by input parameters bufferOnDevice and bufferOnHost. The input parameters workspaceInBytesOnDevice (and workspaceInBytesOnHost) is size in bytes of the device (and host) working space, and it is returned by [Handle.XgesvdrBufferSize].
// If output parameter info = -i (less than zero), the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle).
// Currently, [Handle.Xgesvdr] supports only the default algorithm.
// Algorithms supported by [Handle.Xgesvdr]
//   - [Alg0], the zero value: Default algorithm.
//
// Please visit cuSOLVER Library Samples - [Handle.Xgesvdr] for a code example.
// Remark 1: gesvdr supports n>=m as well.
// Remark 2: the routine returns V, not Vᴴ
// The generic API has five different types, dataTypeA is data type of the matrix A, dataTypeS is data type of the vector S and dataTypeU is data type of the matrix U, dataTypeV is data type of the matrix V, computeType is compute type of the operation. [Handle.Xgesvdr] only supports the following four combinations.
// Valid combination of data type and compute type
//
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - jobu: Specifies options for computing all or part of the matrix U: = ‘S’: the first k columns of U (the left singular vectors) are returned in the array U; = ‘N’: no columns of U (no left singular vectors) are computed
//   - jobv: Specifies options for computing all or part of the matrix V: = ‘S’: the first k rows of V (the right singular vectors) are returned in the array V; = ‘N’: no rows of V (no right singular vectors) are computed
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - k: Rank of the k-SVD decomposition of matrix A. rank is less than min(m,n)
//   - p: Oversampling. The size of the subspace will be (k + p). (k+p) is less than min(m,n)
//   - niters: Number of iteration of power method
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: Array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,m). On exit, the contents of A are destroyed
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - bufferOnDevice: Device workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnDevice bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size in bytes of bufferOnDevice, returned by [Handle.XgesvdrBufferSize]
//   - bufferOnHost: Host workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnHost bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size in bytes of bufferOnHost, returned by [Handle.XgesvdrBufferSize]
//   - dInfo: If info = 0, the operation is successful. If info = -i, the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle)
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( m,n<0 or lda<max(1,m) or ldu<max(1,m) or ldv<max(1,n) ).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgesvdr.
func (h Handle) Xgesvdr(params Params, jobu int8, jobv int8, m int64, n int64, k int64, p int64, niters int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, dataTypeSrand DataType, srand driver.DevicePtr, dataTypeUrand DataType, urand driver.DevicePtr, ldUrand int64, dataTypeVrand DataType, vrand driver.DevicePtr, ldVrand int64, computeType DataType, bufferOnDevice driver.DevicePtr, workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, bufferOnHost uintptr, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint, dInfo driver.DevicePtr) error {
	return xgesvdr(h, params, jobu, jobv, m, n, k, p, niters, dataTypeA, a, lda, dataTypeSrand, srand, dataTypeUrand, urand, ldUrand, dataTypeVrand, vrand, ldVrand, computeType, bufferOnDevice, workspaceInBytesOnDevice, bufferOnHost, workspaceInBytesOnHost, dInfo)
}

// XgesvdrBufferSize returns the workspace sizes, in bytes, for [Handle.Xgesvdr].
//
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - jobu: Specifies options for computing all or part of the matrix U: = ‘S’: the first k columns of U (the left singular vectors) are returned in the array U; = ‘N’: no columns of U (no left singular vectors) are computed
//   - jobv: Specifies options for computing all or part of the matrix V: = ‘S’: the first k rows of V (the right singular vectors) are returned in the array V; = ‘N’: no rows of V (no right singular vectors) are computed
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - k: Rank of the k-SVD decomposition of matrix A. rank is less than min(m,n)
//   - p: Oversampling. The size of the subspace will be (k + p). (k+p) is less than min(m,n)
//   - niters: Number of iteration of power method
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: Array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,m). On exit, the contents of A are destroyed
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size of bufferOnDevice, in bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size of bufferOnHost, in bytes
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( m,n<0 or lda<max(1,m) or ldu<max(1,m) or ldv<max(1,n) ).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgesvdrBufferSize, bound as cusolverDnXgesvdr_bufferSize.
func (h Handle) XgesvdrBufferSize(params Params, jobu int8, jobv int8, m int64, n int64, k int64, p int64, niters int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, dataTypeSrand DataType, srand driver.DevicePtr, dataTypeUrand DataType, urand driver.DevicePtr, ldUrand int64, dataTypeVrand DataType, vrand driver.DevicePtr, ldVrand int64, computeType DataType) (workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint, err error) {
	return xgesvdrBufferSize(h, params, jobu, jobv, m, n, k, p, niters, dataTypeA, a, lda, dataTypeSrand, srand, dataTypeUrand, urand, ldUrand, dataTypeVrand, vrand, ldVrand, computeType)
}

// Xgetrf computes the LU factorization of a m×n matrix.
//
// P*A=L*U, where A is a m×n matrix, P is a permutation matrix, L is a lower triangular matrix with unit diagonal, and U is an upper triangular matrix using the generic API interface.
// If LU factorization failed, i.e. matrix A ( U) is singular, The output parameter info=i indicates U(i,i) = 0.
// If output parameter info = -i (less than zero), the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle).
// If ipiv is null, no pivoting is performed. The factorization is A=L*U, which is not numerically stable.
// No matter LU factorization failed or not, the output parameter ipiv contains pivoting sequence, row i is interchanged with row ipiv(i).
// The user has to provide device and host working spaces which are pointed by input parameters bufferOnDevice and bufferOnHost. The input parameters workspaceInBytesOnDevice (and workspaceInBytesOnHost) is size in bytes of the device (and host) working space, and it is returned by [Handle.XgetrfBufferSize].
// The user can combine [Handle.Xgetrf] and cusolverDnGetrs to complete a linear solver.
// Currently, [Handle.Xgetrf] supports two algorithms. To select legacy implementation, the user has to call [Params.SetAdvOptions].
// Please visit cuSOLVER Library Samples - [Handle.Xgetrf] for a code example.
// Algorithms supported by [Handle.Xgetrf]
//   - [Alg0], the zero value: Default algorithm. The fastest, requires a large workspace of m*n elements.
//   - [Alg1]: Legacy implementation
//
// The generic API has two different types, dataTypeA is data type of the matrix A, computeType is compute type of the operation. [Handle.Xgetrf] only supports the following four combinations.
// Valid combination of data type and compute type
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_R_32F; ComputeType: CUDA_R_32F; Meaning: SGETRF
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_R_64F; ComputeType: CUDA_R_64F; Meaning: DGETRF
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_C_32F; ComputeType: CUDA_C_32F; Meaning: CGETRF
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_C_64F; ComputeType: CUDA_C_64F; Meaning: ZGETRF
//
// Parameters:
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,m)
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - ipiv: Array of size at least min(m,n), containing pivot indices
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - bufferOnDevice: Device workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnDevice bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size in bytes of bufferOnDevice, returned by [Handle.XgetrfBufferSize]
//   - bufferOnHost: Host workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnHost bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size in bytes of bufferOnHost, returned by [Handle.XgetrfBufferSize]
//   - info: If info = 0, the LU factorization is successful. if info = -i, the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle). If info = i, the U(i,i) = 0
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( m,n<0 or lda<max(1,m)).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgetrf.
func (h Handle) Xgetrf(params Params, m int64, n int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, ipiv driver.DevicePtr, computeType DataType, bufferOnDevice driver.DevicePtr, workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, bufferOnHost uintptr, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint, info driver.DevicePtr) error {
	return xgetrf(h, params, m, n, dataTypeA, a, lda, ipiv, computeType, bufferOnDevice, workspaceInBytesOnDevice, bufferOnHost, workspaceInBytesOnHost, info)
}

// XgetrfBufferSize returns the workspace sizes, in bytes, for [Handle.Xgetrf].
//
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix A
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix A
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,m)
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size of bufferOnDevice, in bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size of bufferOnHost, in bytes
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( m,n<0 or lda<max(1,m)).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgetrfBufferSize, bound as cusolverDnXgetrf_bufferSize.
func (h Handle) XgetrfBufferSize(params Params, m int64, n int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, computeType DataType) (workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint, err error) {
	return xgetrfBufferSize(h, params, m, n, dataTypeA, a, lda, computeType)
}

// Xgetrs solves a linear system of multiple right-hand sides.
//
// op(A)*X=B, where A is an n×n matrix, and was LU-factored by [Handle.Xgetrf], that is, lower triangular part of A is L, and upper triangular part (including diagonal elements) of A is U. B is an n×nrhs right-hand side matrix using the generic API interface.
// The input parameter trans is defined by op(A) = A if trans == CUBLAS_OP_N, op(A) = Aᵀ if trans == CUBLAS_OP_T, and op(A) = Aᴴ if trans == CUBLAS_OP_C.
// The input parameter ipiv is an output of [Handle.Xgetrf]. It contains pivot indices, which are used to permutate right-hand sides.
// If output parameter info = -i (less than zero), the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle).
// The user can combine [Handle.Xgetrf] and [Handle.Xgetrs] to complete a linear solver.
// Currently, [Handle.Xgetrs] supports only the default algorithm.
// Please visit cuSOLVER Library Samples - [Handle.Xgetrf] for a code example.
// Algorithms supported by [Handle.Xgetrs]
//   - [Alg0], the zero value: Default algorithm.
//
// The generic API has two different types: dataTypeA is data type of the matrix A and dataTypeB is data type of the matrix B. [Handle.Xgetrs] only supports the following four combinations:
// Valid combination of data type and compute type
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_R_32F; dataTypeB: CUDA_R_32F; Meaning: SGETRS
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_R_64F; dataTypeB: CUDA_R_64F; Meaning: DGETRS
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_C_32F; dataTypeB: CUDA_C_32F; Meaning: CGETRS
//   - DataTypeA: CUDA_C_64F; dataTypeB: CUDA_C_64F; Meaning: ZGETRS
//
// Parameters:
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - trans: Operation op(A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - n: Number of rows and columns of matrix A
//   - nrhs: Number of right-hand sides
//   - dataTypeA: Data type of array A
//   - a: Array of dimension lda * n with lda is not less than max(1,n)
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - ipiv: Array of size at least n, containing pivot indices
//   - dataTypeB: Data type of array B
//   - b: array of dimension ldb * nrhs with ldb is not less than max(1,n)
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - info: If info = 0, the operation is successful. If info = -i, the i-th parameter is wrong (not counting handle)
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( n<0 or lda<max(1,n) or ldb<max(1,n)).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXgetrs.
func (h Handle) Xgetrs(params Params, trans Operation, n int64, nrhs int64, dataTypeA DataType, a driver.DevicePtr, lda int64, ipiv driver.DevicePtr, dataTypeB DataType, b driver.DevicePtr, ldb int64, info driver.DevicePtr) error {
	return xgetrs(h, params, trans, n, nrhs, dataTypeA, a, lda, ipiv, dataTypeB, b, ldb, info)
}

// Xlarft forms the triangular factor T of a real block reflector H of order n, which is defined as a product of k elementary reflectors.
//
// If:
// Only storev == CUBLAS_STOREV_COLUMNWISE is supported, which indicates that the vector defining the elementary reflector H(i) is stored in the i-th column of the array V, and H=I−V*T*Vᵀ (H=I−V*T*Vᴴ for complex types).
// The user has to provide device and host working spaces which are pointed by input parameters bufferOnDevice and bufferOnHost. The input parameters workspaceInBytesOnDevice (and workspaceInBytesOnHost) is size in bytes of the device (and host) working space, and it is returned by [Handle.XlarftBufferSize].
// Currently, only n >= k scenario is supported.
// The generic API has four different types:
// [Handle.Xlarft] only supports the following four combinations.
// Valid combinations of data types and compute types
//
//   - params: Structure with information collected by [Params.SetAdvOptions]
//   - direct: Specifies the order in which the elementary reflectors are multiplied to form the block reflector
//   - storev: Specifies how the vectors which define the elementary reflectors are stored
//   - n: The order of the block reflector H. n >= 0
//   - k: The order of the triangular factor T (= the number of elementary reflectors). k >= 1
//   - dataTypeV: Data type of array V
//   - v: The matrix V of dimension lda * k
//   - ldv: Leading dimension of the array V. ldv >= max(1,n)
//   - dataTypeTau: Data type of array tau
//   - tau: Dimension k. tau(i) must contain the scalar factor of the elementary reflector H(i)
//   - dataTypeT: Data type of array T
//   - t: Dimension ldt * k. The k×k triangular factor T of the block reflector. If direct == CUBLAS_DIRECT_FORWARD, T is upper triangular; if direct == CUBLAS_DIRECT_BACKWARD, T is lower triangular
//   - ldt: The leading dimension of the array T. ldt >= k
//   - computeType: Data type of computation
//   - bufferOnDevice: Device workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnDevice bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnDevice: Size in bytes of bufferOnDevice, returned by [Handle.XlarftBufferSize]
//   - bufferOnHost: Host workspace. Array of type void of size workspaceInBytesOnHost bytes
//   - workspaceInBytesOnHost: Size in bytes of bufferOnHost, returned by [Handle.XlarftBufferSize]
//
// Errors:
//   - [ErrInternalError]: An internal operation failed.
//   - [ErrInvalidValue]: Invalid parameters were passed ( n == 0, k > n, or storev == CUBLAS_STOREV_ROWWISE).
//   - [ErrNotInitialized]: The library was not initialized.
//
// Wraps cusolverDnXlarft.
func (h Handle) Xlarft(params Params, direct DirectMode, storev StorevMode, n int64, k int64, dataTypeV DataType, v driver.DevicePtr, ldv int64, dataTypeTau DataType, tau driver.DevicePtr, dataTypeT DataType, t driver.DevicePtr, ldt int64, computeType DataType, bufferOnDevice driver.DevicePtr, workspaceInBytesOnDevice uint, bufferOnHost uintptr, workspaceInBytesOnHost uint) error {
	return xlarft(h, params, direct, storev, n, k, dataTypeV, v, ldv, dataTypeTau, tau, dataTypeT, t, ldt, computeType, bufferOnDevice, workspaceInBytesOnDevice, bufferOnHost, workspaceInBytesOnHost)
}

// XlarftBufferSize returns the workspace sizes, in bytes, for [Handle.Xlarft].
